      {
        "id": 137348,
        "name": "payprplayn",
        "username": "payprplayn",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/b2d939/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-15T21:50:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I teleport a lot, too, but not really to run away. &nbsp;Instead, I tend to leave in Teleporter and Battlesuit and just try to remove scenario markers as fast as possible. &nbsp;The scenario is basically a race, and your reward for incapacitating heroes isn't as valuable as the actions it costs to do so. &nbsp;The exception is if I start the turn knowing that I can either get to the next marker with a move action rather than a teleport, or that I won't be going to the next marker this turn anyway, I'll put in kinetic redistributor in place of teleporter in hopes I might get an incap at some point without having to spend actions on attacking. &nbsp;The way I see it, you just have to live long enough to remove your marker quota. &nbsp;You can try to achieve this by either living longer, or removing markers faster. &nbsp;I think the latter is more fun.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:13:42.030Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
